From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:50:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm-vma-drop-mm-asynchronously-in-vma_start_read-fix-2

comment fixup, per Suren

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/CAJuCfpEmFEX5iqLw_c94a97rVrC+xBWpKnO4rVpeDgkUfAPq7Q@mail.gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: "Lorenzo Stoakes (ARM)" <ljs@kernel.org>
Cc: Suren Baghdasaryan <surenb@google.com>

 mm/mmap_lock.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
 mm/mmap_lock.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/mmap_lock.c b/mm/mmap_lock.c
index 22132f87e90f..9f2c66df0a89 100644
--- a/mm/mmap_lock.c
+++ b/mm/mmap_lock.c
@@ -304,7 +304,7 @@ static struct vm_area_struct *vma_start_read(struct mm_struct *mm,
 	 * is dropped and before rcuwait_wake_up(mm) is called. Grab it before
 	 * releasing vma->vm_refcnt.
 	 */
-	other_mm = vma->vm_mm; /* use a copy as vma can be freed after we drop vm_refcnt */
+	other_mm = vma->vm_mm; /* use a copy as vma can be reused after we drop vm_refcnt */
 
 	mmgrab(other_mm);
 	vma_refcount_put(vma);
-- 
